INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION — compose #461 (perf/borrow-cost) + #460 (perf/t8-scaling)
====================================================================================

Host      Apple M4 Pro, 8 P-cores + 4 E-cores (12 logical), Darwin 25.5.0.
Base      main 6c17d8c. BOTH branches merge-base at 6c17d8c exactly — verified
          with `git merge-base`, and `git log 6c17d8c..<branch>` shows nothing
          on main that either branch is missing. The "measured against a stale
          branch point" failure mode of the previous round (#459: two branches
          targeting a wide path #458 had already removed) DOES NOT APPLY here.
Compose   `git merge perf/borrow-cost` then `git merge perf/t8-scaling` —
          NO CONFLICTS. Both carry the same `style: cargo fmt` reflow.
Build     cargo build --release, default features, NO -C target-cpu=native.
Timing    NO `nice` on any timed run. Two-point wall fit (2 and 20 frames,
          beta = (hi-lo)/18) so process startup drops out.
Method    scripts/perf/verify_gap.sh, rotating-order interleaved, dav1d 1.5.4
          measured IN THE SAME SWEEP. n=7 for the gap, n=5 for the
          decomposition. STRICT idle gate: 5 cells were DISCARDED and re-run
          when a foreign process crossed 25%; **all 224 committed gap rows and
          all 80 decomposition rows carry foreign=0**.
Files     verify_compose5_gap_2026-08-08.tsv      224 raw rows (4 arms x 8 cells x 7)
          verify_compose5_decomp_2026-08-08.tsv    80 raw rows (4 arms x 4 cells x 5)
          verify_compose5_buckets_2026-08-08.txt   sample self-time, base + head


VERDICT: the composition is sound, pixel-inert, and materially faster at every
cell — and the ~1.30x bar is met at NO thread count. Best cell 1.368x.


