8. THREE THINGS THAT ARE BROKEN ON `main` AND ARE NOT THESE BRANCHES' FAULT
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(a) `tests/decode_permutations.rs` — 16 of 19 tests FAIL ON AARCH64, on
    UNMODIFIED main, under the exact CI invocation
    (`cargo nextest run --no-default-features --features "bitdepth_8,bitdepth_16"
    --release --test decode_permutations`): `called Option::unwrap() on a None
    value` at `src/safe_simd/mc_arm.rs:5931` (`Arm64::summon().unwrap()`) and
    `src/safe_simd/filmgrain_arm.rs`. Composed head: the SAME 16 of 19, same
    sites. **The token-permutation bit-identity gate is dead on aarch64 and CI
    cannot see it: `.github/workflows/ci.yml:245` pins that job to
    `ubuntu-latest`, where the `*_arm.rs` code paths do not exist.** A gate that
    passes only because it is never run on the architecture where it fails.
    `--test-threads=1` does NOT fix it; the file's own header attributing this
    class of failure to parallelism is a red herring here.
(b) `cargo fmt --all --check` FAILS on main at two sites
    (`tracker_shard.rs:1824`, `loopfilter.rs:5257`) — which is why the `Format`
    CI job is red on 6c17d8c. Both branches' `style: cargo fmt` commits are
    exactly this fix, so THE COMPOSITION TURNS THAT JOB GREEN (`cargo fmt --all
    --check` rc=0 on the composed tree).
(c) `cargo clippy --no-default-features --features "bitdepth_8,bitdepth_16"
    -- -D warnings` fails identically on main and on head:
    `method 'bit' is never used` (`src/ablate.rs:83`). Pre-existing; not fixed
    here. `cargo clippy --release -p rav1d-disjoint-mut --all-targets` is clean.
Also re-confirmed: `test-vectors/bench/photo_4k.avif` is gitignored, so
`mt_stress` hard-fails in any fresh worktree until it is copied in.


9. WHERE #461's OWN NARRATIVE IS INCOMPLETE (not wrong — incomplete)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Its per-increment attribution table is t=1 ONLY, and its headline mechanism —
"`mask == 0` skips the block arithmetic entirely... this is the big one" —
CANNOT fire on the hot picture planes at t>1. `src/lib.rs:181` calls
`set_parallelism(n_tc)`, `n_tc > 1` raises ACTIVE_SHARDS to 128, and
`mask_for(len >= SHARD_MIN_LEN)` then returns 127. So on a multi-threaded decode
the skip applies only to the ~1,027 sub-64-KiB instances. The measured t>1 wins
(0.910-0.926 head/base) are real and are bought by the OTHER four mechanisms
(per-slot flags, the frameless leaf, straight-line `live_mask`, straight-line
`alloc`). Nothing to fix; the attribution table just does not cover the cells
it is quoted next to.


10. NOT DONE HERE
------------------
- x86_64: NOT MEASURED, and this composition is the change most likely to
  behave differently there (two `lock`-prefixed RMWs per borrow pair removed;
  on x86 those are full fences, on M4 LSE they are cheap). #461 says the same.
  Do not extrapolate the aarch64 ratios.
- Only `v4k_8tile` and `v4k_8tile_10b`. No `v4k_1tile`, no small sizes, no
  12bpc perf cell (12bpc correctness is covered by the corpus).
- Miri was not run (`crates/rav1d-disjoint-mut/tests/aligned_miri.rs` exists;
  the `disjoint-mut CI` Miri job is among the 6 already red on main).
- #460's own probe-tasktime numbers (occupancy 7.143/8, the 12% post-tile tail,
  the blockshift and shards-256 ladders) were NOT re-run. Its two load-bearing
  claims that I could check independently — the untracked/plain ratios and the
  dav1d 6.83x correction — both reproduced.
